  "meaning": "A seven-position precision register holds independent removable inserts: a deep book cassette, thick token comb, engraved document block, oxide-inlaid letterpress block, hinged catalog books, deep branch gate, and preview housing. Every upright insert has an oxide accent and a distinct three-dimensional section. Keyed sockets, flush hex fasteners, small locating pins, replaceable feet, and a copper registration slide make the fixture mechanically explicit. The inserts are independent tools, not a processing chain. Detailed machined construction, actual recessed marks, separate fasteners, brushed polished steel, dark red-brown granular corrosion islands with broken oxide rims, pitted normal relief and dull oxidized metal between crusts, graphite interiors, directional softbox reflections, and genuine transparent negative space.",
